                "text": "ISSUE_KIND: road_damage\nISSUE: Major road pavement collapse and sinkhole next to a storm drain\nDETAILS: The photo shows a large section of concrete street pavement caved in above a deep subterranean void near a storm drain, with a wooden barrier structure and a signpost inside the hole. The user note states that the road caved in next to the storm drain about 4 feet across, in the Adelphi Woods Homeowners Association area on Tecumseh Street.\nORGANIZATION: Prince George's County Department of Public Works and Transportation\nDEPARTMENT: Office of Highway Maintenance\nWHY: The location on Tecumseh Street in Adelphi is in an unincorporated area of Prince George's County. The Prince George's County Department of Public Works and Transportation (DPW&T) Office of Highway Maintenance is responsible for maintaining County-maintained roadways, including repairing sinkholes and structural road damage.\nCOVERAGE_QUOTE: \"As part of the Prince George's County Roadway Preservation Program, maintenance includes the repair of sinkholes and potholes, shoulder repair, removal and replacement of concrete curb and gutter, sidewalks, driveway aprons, the installation of underdrains, the installation and/or upgrade of handicapped access ramps per ADA standards and the repair/resurfacing of the roadway pavement.\"\nCOVERAGE_URL: https://www.princegeorgescountymd.gov/388/Office-of-Highway-Maintenance\nREPORTING_URL: https://www.pgc311.com\nOFFICIAL_WEBSITE: https://www.princegeorgescountymd.gov/1000/Public-Works-Transportation\nEMAIL: unknown\nPHONE: 311 | https://www.princegeorgescountymd.gov/388/Office-of-Highway-Maintenance\nPHOTO_LOOKS_DAYTIME: yes\nNOTE_SAYS_LIGHT_OUT: no\nSOURCES:\nhttps://www.princegeorgescountymd.gov/388/Office-of-Highway-Maintenance\nhttps://www.princegeorgescountymd.gov/1000/Public-Works-Transportation\nhttps://www.princegeorgescountymd.gov/3981/Potholes\nhttps://www.princegeorgescountymd.gov/1018/PGC311",
